{%- macro whyTarget(tool = "Vite") -%}
{{ tool }} compiles CSS for browsers older than Cirth supports. That process
rewrites `light-dark()` colours. The page can still follow the system theme,
but a `data-theme` region may fail to force the other colour scheme. Set
{{ tool }} to Cirth's browser floor below. [Compatibility](/compatibility)
explains the transformation and its limits.
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro checkIt(lowers = false, fix = "check the CSS target above") -%}
Put this forced-dark region in a page or component that uses the global
stylesheet:

```html
<section data-theme="dark">
  <article>
    <p>Dark, whatever the system scheme is.</p>
  </article>
</section>
```

{% if lowers %}Build for production, then {% else %}Run the app, then {% endif %}open
the page while the system uses a light theme. A dark article proves that
Cirth loaded and that `data-theme="dark"` is working. It remains dark when
the system switches to a dark theme.{% if lowers %} If the article follows
the surrounding page instead, the build rewrote Cirth's colours: {{ fix }}.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

